pygfx is a render engine for Python built on WebGPU (via wgpu-py). It provides
a high-level, scene-graph based API for 2D and 3D visualization: meshes, points,
lines, images, volumes, text, cameras, lights, and PBR materials, with
custom shaders. Rendering targets are supplied by rendercanvas (glfw, Qt,
Jupyter, offscreen).
